| `secrets.scanner.rev` | string | `v8.30.1` | one path part (no `/`, `\` or NUL, no leading `.` or surrounding whitespace): the release `secrets.scanner.release_assets` pins | `scripts/scan_secrets.py` and `scripts/install_scanner.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.rev` row | Sets the scanner release `make secrets-install` installs under, as one directory of `<install_root>/<name>/<rev>/<name>`, so a value that is not one path part is exit 14 before any fetch, and the release the record must name; change it with `secrets.scanner.release_url` and `secrets.scanner.release_assets`, then run `make secrets-install`. A record naming another rev is exit 11 until then. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.rev = "v8.30.1"` to stderr. | fetching anything by itself: the archive is the one `secrets.scanner.release_assets` pins | always |
